  "id": "Compound::DB01028 - Gene::55879",
  "verbalization": "Methoxyflurane is likely to interact with Gabrq through a mechanism involving the Gaba-a receptor. The evidence suggests that Methoxyflurane binds to Gabrd or Gabre, which in turn participate in Gaba-a receptor activity. This activity is then recognized by Gabrq, indicating a potential regulatory or functional relationship between Methoxyflurane and Gabrq. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be clarified. The involvement of multiple receptor subtypes (Gabra4, Gabrd, and Gabre) highlights the complexity of the pathway, with Gabrq possibly acting as a downstream effector or modulator of Gaba-a receptor function. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Gaba-a receptors in mediating the effects of Methoxyflurane, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism.",
